{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>I will cause all My goodness to pass before your face.</b> It should have said לפניך, as it says, ״וקראתי בשם ה׳ לפניך״. By way of the plain sense (peshat), it seems to me to say that it comes to allude to what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: it was difficult for Moses regarding the thirteen attributes, that He mentioned 'slow to anger' (ארך אפים) and did not mention 'slow to wrath' (ארך אף). The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: 'for the righteous and for the wicked.' Moses said to Him: 'Master of the universe, let the wicked perish!' He said to him: 'By your life, you will need this matter when a sin occurs.' When the sin of the spies happened, he began (Numbers 14:17–18): ״ועתה יגדל נא כח ה׳ כאשר דברת לאמר ה׳ ארך אפים״ — that is, remember that utterance You spoke to me, both for the righteous and for the wicked. From this He needed to say על פניך, to allude to this utterance which He was destined to make heard to him against his will." "<b>Or</b> we may further say that He mentioned על פניך — that is, 'I will cause all My goodness to pass over your face,' and from it you will be elevated, so that the light radiates upon your face; and this is the excellence of the shining of the face (קרון פנים), which he merited from the splitting of the Rock (נקרת הצור), as the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: 'I will cause all My goodness to pass before your face' — טובי and כל טובי: the attribute of goodness and the attribute of punishment." "<b>And I will grant grace to whom I grant grace.</b> At that hour the Holy One, blessed be He, showed Moses all the treasuries of the reward of the righteous, each one according to his deeds. He would ask: 'This treasury — whose is it?' and He would say to him: 'It belongs to the masters of Torah.' And: 'This treasury — whose is it?' — 'It belongs to those who honor them.' Afterward He showed him a treasury greater than these. He said: 'Master of the universe, this great treasury — whose is it?' He said to him: 'Whoever has good deeds — I give him from his treasuries; and whoever does not — gratuitously I act and give him from this one,' as it is said: ״וחנותי את אשר אחון״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'I will cause all My goodness to pass before your face' — this goodness is what is written: ״וראית את אחורי״, and in its explanation: everything that is 'My goodness,' and this is (Exodus 19:5): ״כי לי כל הארץ״; (1 Chronicles 29:11): ״כי כל בשמים ובארץ״, and this is clear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:49.356531013Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}